From: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
Subject: [PATCH] dts: orangepi-zero: use the physical arch timer (no firmware CNTVOFF)

Under the SPL Falcon boot nothing runs U-Boot's non-secure init, so
CNTVOFF is never written. cpu0 and a freshly powered cpu1 (a cold boot,
or a cpu1 that PSCI had power-gated during a U-Boot proper boot) then
disagree on the virtual counter, the clock jumps by thousands of
seconds between cores, the RCU grace-period kthread never wakes and the
watchdog resets the board. The ramoops console of such a boot shows
"clocksource: Switched to clocksource arch_sys_counter" stamped 5409 s
while the other core is at 0.05 s, then the RCU stall. Warm reboots
survived only because the previous U-Boot boot had zeroed CNTVOFF on
both cores and the watchdog reset kept it.

The A23/A33 DT property for firmware that leaves the timer registers
alone makes the kernel use the physical counter and timer, which have
no offset, and request both the secure and non-secure physical PPIs,
so a U-Boot proper (non-secure) boot keeps working too. The rate comes
from clock-frequency. Applies after 0010.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [appliance-specific]
Signed-off-by: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h2-plus-orangepi-zero.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h2-plus-orangepi-zero.dts
@@ -308,3 +308,16 @@
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 };
+
+/* usb-proxy appliance: without U-Boot's non-secure init nothing sets
+ * CNTVOFF, so a freshly powered cpu1 (cold boot, or after PSCI power-off
+ * on a U-Boot proper boot) carries a different virtual-counter offset than
+ * cpu0 and the kernel's clock jumps between cores: "clocksource switched"
+ * at 5409 s on one CPU, RCU stall, watchdog reset (the "last Falcon boot
+ * died" fallback, 2026-10-03). This is the A23/A33 property for the same
+ * situation: use the offset-free physical counter and both physical PPIs,
+ * which also works for a U-Boot proper (non-secure) boot. */
+&{/timer} {
+	clock-frequency = <24000000>;
+	arm,cpu-registers-not-fw-configured;
+};
